<!--
  Launcher icon, monochrome layer for themed icons. Original work,
  Copyright (C) 2026 Eyed.

  A separate drawing, not `@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground` pointed at a
  second time. The template did exactly that — background, foreground *and*
  monochrome all resolved to the same two files — and it is the usual mistake,
  because the foreground is designed against a known background and the
  monochrome layer is not:

  * The colour mark has two tones. The prompt is bone, the cursor is amber, and
    the ~8.6 units of clear space between them is enough *because the two
    shapes are different colours*. Flatten both to one tint, as the themed
    launcher does, and that gap is the only thing left separating a chevron
    from a rectangle. Here it is opened to ~10.7 units.
  * A single-tone glyph loses the contrast that made the strokes read, so the
    chevron is drawn heavier: 9.2 units against the colour version's 8.4.
  * Themed icons sit on a solid system plate with no tile of their own, and a
    glyph tuned to fill a coloured tile looks oversized on one. The whole mark
    is inset ~5% (ink spans 30.4..77.6 horizontally, 32.1..75.9 vertically,
    still centred on (54,54), furthest point 30.3 of the 33-unit safe radius).

  The colour is `#FF000000` because the system re-tints this layer to the
  theme's foreground colour and only the alpha channel survives the trip.
  Black is what Google's own themed assets use, so a launcher that skipped the
  tint would still show a legible dark glyph on a light plate rather than
  nothing at all.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:pathData="M35,36.7 L47.9,54 L35,71.3"
        android:strokeColor="#FF000000"
        android:strokeWidth="9.2"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000" />
    <path
        android:pathData="M66.4,43.8 L74.4,43.8 A3.2,3.2 0 0 1 77.6,47 L77.6,61 A3.2,3.2 0 0 1 74.4,64.2 L66.4,64.2 A3.2,3.2 0 0 1 63.2,61 L63.2,47 A3.2,3.2 0 0 1 66.4,43.8 Z"
        android:fillColor="#FF000000" />
</vector>
